{"id":357,"flavor":[{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"Bunches of delicious fruit grow around its neck. In warm areas, many ranches raise Tropius."},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"The bunches of fruit growing around the necks of Tropius in Alola are especially sweet compared to those in other regions."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Sapphire"],"text":"Children of the southern tropics eat as snacks the fruit that grows in bunches around the neck of Tropius. This Pokémon flies by flapping the leaves on its back as if they were wings."},{"games":["Omega Ruby","Ruby"],"text":"The bunches of fruit around Tropius’s neck are very popular with children. This Pokémon loves fruit, and eats it continuously. Apparently, its love for fruit resulted in its own outgrowth of fruit."},{"games":["Y","SoulSilver","HeartGold"],"text":"The bunch of fruit around its neck ripens twice a year and is delicious. It’s a highly favored tropical snack."},{"games":["X","White 2","Black 2"],"text":"It flies by flapping its broad leaves and gives the sweet, delicious fruit around its neck to children."},{"games":["White","Black","Platinum"],"text":"Delicious fruits grew out from around its neck because it always ate the same kind of fruit."},{"games":["Pearl","Diamond"],"text":"Because it continually ate only its favorite fruit, the fruit started growing around its neck."},{"games":["LeafGreen","FireRed"],"text":"It lives in tropical jungles. The bunch of fruit around its neck is delicious. The fruit grows twice a year."},{"games":["Emerald"],"text":"It flies by flapping its broad leaves. The bunch of fruit that grows around its neck is deliciously sweet. In the spring, it scatters pollen from its neck."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Chlorophyll","hidden":false,"description":"Boosts the Pokémon's Speed stat in harsh sunlight."},{"name":"Solar Power","hidden":false,"description":"In harsh sunlight, the Pokémon's Sp. Atk stat is boosted, but its HP decreases every turn."},{"name":"Harvest","hidden":true,"descr